  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_006: multimodal/multiprofile/pca_n2000/resnet50/avgpool/concat → 0.619 acc), evidence is extremely sparse. The most architecturally impactful untested dimension within this exact family is the aggregation method. Config_007 changes only aggregation from avgpool to transformer while holding all other parameters constant (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat), providing a clean single-variable comparison. Transformer aggregation enables attention-based modeling of inter-cellular relationships, which is a fundamentally more expressive operation than mean pooling and could yield a meaningful accuracy gain for cellular profiling. Clarifying whether transformer aggregation helps is a high-value uncertainty to resolve early, as it will inform whether to invest remaining budget in transformer-based configurations across other encoder/fusion combinations or to focus on avgpool variants."
}

